<title>AUSTRALIA: RTRS-Macquarie plans infrastructure trust.</title>
<headline>RTRS-Macquarie plans infrastructure trust.</headline>
<dateline>SYDNEY 1996-10-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>Investment Bank Macquarie Bank Ltd will launch a A$300 million to A$400 million infrastructure trust later this month, banking industry sources.</p>
<p>The trust will be called the Infrastructure Trust of Australia and would be partly paid initially, with the first stage offering A$1.00 units for 55 cents and the second stage of 45 cents being paid within two years, the sources said.</p>
<p>The trust would buy stakes in Hills Motorway Group and Transurban City Link Ltd, they said. Macquarie said it could not comment under Australian Securities Commission rules.</p>
<p>-- Sydney Newsroom 61-2 373-1800</p>
</text>
